    "raw": "Let's denote the price Tommy bought his first house for as \\( x \\). According to the problem, the current value of his home is 25% more than what he bought it for, which can be expressed as \\( 1.25x \\).\n\nTommy sells his home for \\( 1.25x \\) and uses this money to buy a new house that costs $500,000. Since he can only pay 25% of the new house's cost with the money from selling his first house, he needs to take a loan for the remaining 75%.\n\nThe equation representing the situation is:\n\\[ 1.25x = 0.25 \\times 500,000 \\]\n\nSolving for \\( x \\):\n\\[ 1.25x = 125,000 \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{125,000}{1.25} \\]\n\\[ x = 100,000 \\]\n\nSo, Tommy bought his first house for $100,000.\n\nFINAL: 100000",
